# Code-only repository.
# Everything is ignored EXCEPT source code and the small text files Unity needs to open the project.
# Not in git: Unity cache (Library, Temp, Logs), builds, the listing kit, 3D models, Blender files,
# audio, images, fonts and scenes. Keep those backed up elsewhere.

# 1. Ignore everything at the top level...
/*

# 2. ...then let these back in.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md

# Python asset tools (voices, music, logo, buildings)
!/Tools/
/Tools/*
!/Tools/*.py

# Package list, so Unity installs the same packages
!/Packages/
/Packages/*
!/Packages/manifest.json
!/Packages/packages-lock.json

# Project settings (small text files)
!/ProjectSettings/

# Game code: only C# scripts and their .meta files (the .meta keeps each script's ID stable)
!/Assets/
/Assets/*
!/Assets/Game/
/Assets/Game/*
!/Assets/Game/README.md
!/Assets/Game/Scripts/
!/Assets/Game/Editor/
/Assets/Game/Scripts/**/*.*
/Assets/Game/Editor/**/*.*
!/Assets/Game/Scripts/**/*.cs
!/Assets/Game/Scripts/**/*.cs.meta
!/Assets/Game/Editor/**/*.cs
!/Assets/Game/Editor/**/*.cs.meta

# 3. Never commit these, wherever they are
.DS_Store
*.blend1
*.tmp
*.csproj
*.sln
*.slnx

# Settings left by removed packages
/ProjectSettings/Packages/com.unity.ai.assistant/
